# Project constraints

Follow these constraints when editing the Helm codebase.

## Navigation

- **Do not change navigation.** Leave the app shell and marketing routing as-is. Do not add, remove, or rename top-level nav items (e.g. Helm | Quarter | Outcomes | Settings) or marketing routes without explicit user request.

## Data

- **Use existing mock data only.** Read from `lib/mock/` (e.g. `mockData.ts`, `feature-ideas.ts`) and shared types in `lib/types`. Do not add new mock modules or seed data unless the user explicitly asks for new features or content that require it.

## Styling

- **Keep styling aligned with shadcn + Tailwind.** Use design tokens from `app/globals.css` (e.g. `text-foreground`, `bg-card`, `border-border`, `text-muted-foreground`) and existing components in `components/ui/`. Prefer Tailwind utility classes; avoid adding new CSS files or inline styles that bypass the design system.

## Testing

- **User-visible contract.** When adding or editing front-end tests, anchor queries and assertions to what users see and can do (roles, labels, outcomes), not to translation keys, component implementation, CSS class names, or internal state shape.
- **Implementation refactors should stay green** if the experience is unchanged; **user-visible regressions should fail** tests (including intentional copy changes, which require updating expectations deliberately).
- **Real layout and obscured elements** are best validated in browser-level tests (e.g. Playwright); JSDOM is not a full layout engine.
- **Details:** see `.cursor/rules/frontend-testing.mdc` for query priority, examples, and links.
